course: dictionary
lesson: 7099
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it. The word peacock is a good example: it can name a large bird, a butterfly, or a person who shows off.
explain: «The peacock spread its tail into a huge blue-green fan.» Here peacock means a large male bird, because of the tail and the fan. «Ben is such a peacock, checking his hair in every window.» Here peacock means a vain person, because checking his hair is a clue about showing off.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits the sentence? Try each meaning in place of the word and see which one makes sense. Then use the clues around the word to choose the right one.
fact: Peacock is a noun. A peacock is a large male bird, and the female is a peahen. Both are called peafowl.
fact: «Peacock» can also mean a vain person, someone who shows off how they look.
fact: A peacock butterfly is a butterfly with big eye spots on its wings.
fact: «Proud as a peacock» describes someone who is very pleased with themselves.
exercise: «The peacock spread its tail into a huge fan.» In this sentence, what is a peacock? | *A large male bird with a long, colourful tail | A butterfly with eye spots | A female bird that is plain brown | A vain person who shows off
exercise: «Ben is such a peacock, he spends ages checking his hair in the mirror.» What does peacock mean here? | A large male bird | A bird that cannot fly | *A vain person who shows off how they look | A butterfly with eye spots
exercise: Which phrase means someone is very pleased with themselves? | *Proud as a peacock | Quiet as a mouse | Busy as a bee | Cold as ice
test: «A peacock butterfly flashes big eye spots to scare away birds.» What is a peacock butterfly? | *A butterfly with eye spots on its wings | A large male bird with a long tail | A vain person who shows off | A moth that flies at night
test: «The peahen is plain brown, so she is hard to see on her nest.» What is a peahen? | A vain person who shows off | A male peacock with a big tail | *A female peafowl | A butterfly with eye spots
exam: Why does a dictionary give several meanings for peacock? | Because peacock is a verb and a noun | Because peacock is two different words that look the same and cannot be linked | Because peacocks come in many sizes | *Because the word can name a bird, a butterfly, or a vain person
